# rm368, the halfway shout (Docs/Design/84). Exported from ridgemere3 at revision 1: edit it in Atlas or the DM, or as a draft through tools/mantle_load.py.
mantle rm368
revision 1
state ready
dialect plain
accent none
tier standard
written_for rmx_ivo_pitchridge
written_by codex
title the halfway shout
fits stage=adult|old
prefers job=laborer
traits temper=even talk=chatty warmth=cold humour=none honesty=guarded piety=ordinary drive=steady
quirk climbs_in_pairs_and_saves_a_cry_for_the_odd_step
likes oatcakes riddles market_bustle thunder
dislikes early_bells rats
fears a_knock_before_the_new_moon
hopes an_oatcake_bought_with_unpromised_coin
topics work +0.6 pastimes +0.4 prices +0.4 weather +0.2
styles comfort=indirect gossip=selective refuse=equivocal tease=none
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# climbs two treads with every breath, talks readily across a market and keeps one unanswered question behind the teeth.

words
oath! = Halve my top stair | Crack my oat in two
saying! = Two steps cover a distance but never a debt | Price the cloth before the cry
landing = a half-landing | a turn of stair
cry = a clear call | a rising cry
bale = a red-tied bale | a squat bundle
rag = a long rag strip | a crooked corner
moon = a narrow moon rim | a brass-coloured crescent
cake = a plain oatcake | a crumbly oat round
purse = my inside purse | a sewn pouch
slate = the market slate | a public board
rail = a stout stair rail | a worn handrail
stepedge = the near stair edge | a chipped nosing
scrape = a light scratching | a scurry in the wall
riddle = an unfinished question | a neat little riddle
drum = a roll of thunder | a long growl overhead

any
opinion @1 houses against 2 : I'd like a factor obliged to climb as many steps for a payment as the wolf finding it.
opinion @1 sump for 1 : A low room still gives a call a high roof if enough of us hear it.
opinion @1 merchants mixed 1 : My voice can carry the marked price. Making the price fair is a different line of work.
opinion @1 dole for 2 : A wolf with nothing left for supper ought to get a portion without answering a riddle.
opinion @1 festivals mixed 1 : A crowd can be glorious when the coin in it has already paid the night's rent.
opinion @1 watch against 1 : A pair of heavy feet can stop a whole stairful of quiet conversation.

grown
line @1 greet : There's a gap beside the calling place. | Stand clear of my market elbow.
line @1 greet.return : Welcome made it in one breath. Here's mine. | I heard even the low end of that greeting.
line @1 again.open : Back up the odd step again.
line @1 farewell : Take the stair by the sound edge. | Keep the rest of your day's price to yourself.
line @1 farewell.return : And two good steps for every tiring one. | My parting's light enough to carry.
line @1 react.news : Let me hear what the crowd couldn't swallow. | Tell it at the pitch it started on.
line @1 react.news.new : No answer for that in my pocket yet.
line @1 react.news.known : I've heard the return cry on that account.
line @1 react.news.doubt : The riddle and its answer haven't travelled together.
line @1 react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|assault] : I'd drop my voice for the wolves carrying that hurt.
line @1 react.news.glad [topic.kind=birth|marriage|work] : That goes up the stair two steps at once.
line @1 ask.how : Have you bought yourself much quiet in all the noise?
line @1 answer.how : I've another call left. That's about my measure.
line @1 sympathise : Nobody else needs to hear it from me.
line @1 reassure : You needn't see the whole stair to step onto the first dry board.
line @1 refuse : There's a call I owe an answer before that one.
line @1 accept_decline : No sale. We can leave the price talk there.
line @1 preclose : I've still got the last odd step of my own errand to take.
line @1 accept_preclose : Go get clear before my next voice carries.
line @1 ack : I've caught the answer under the noise.
scene exchange1
when topic=work self.job=laborer
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I call the pattern first and the price on the turn. | I've got a short cry for a crowded hour.
b : What turn? | Does it leave anything out?
a : The buyer's head. No good pricing a sleeve to a departing ear. | Only what the eye can settle from the front of the stall.

scene exchange2
when topic=travel
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Two treads per stride unless there's an odd one. | I remember a bad stair by which knee it meets.
b : Where does the spare tread fit? | Wouldn't a mark be easier?
a : Keep it for the breath after the climb. | A mark can wear away between market days.

scene exchange3
when topic=food self.likes=oatcakes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : My oatcake gets split in half before the climb. | I like the oatcake with one burnt speck.
b : Why not eat it walking? | What's the special taste?
a : I like knowing a whole half's still waiting behind my back teeth. | Toast. Only takes one speck to point it out.

scene exchange4
when topic=pastimes self.likes=riddles
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I made a riddle from a stair that's one tread short. | A riddle can ride inside a price call.
b : How do you solve it? | Wouldn't that confuse the buyer?
a : Look up. A short step has borrowed the landing. | Only if the price is my question. The price I tell straight.

scene exchange5
when topic=prices self.likes=market_bustle
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A crowded market throws my call back changed. | I like two rows talking across one lane.
b : Who changes it? | What's there to like?
a : Ten mouths trying to remember whether I said striped or spotted. | I can walk through ten different deals without entering one.

scene exchange6
when topic=weather self.likes=thunder
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A thunder roll puts the buyers quiet for a breath. | I save a long breath when the clouds darken.
b : Do you fill it with a cry? | Meant to outsound thunder?
a : No. That's the only caller in the sky I don't interrupt. | Meant to be heard in the pause that comes behind it.

scene exchange7
when topic=day self.dislikes=early_bells
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : The early bell has an account with my pillow. | I count the morning bells in pairs.
b : Overdue again? | And the odd stroke?
a : Always wants paying before my feet agree to rise. | I pull the cover over that one.

scene exchange8
when topic=animals self.dislikes=rats
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Rat teeth can set a whole oatcake rattling in its tin. | I stop on the stair when I hear scratching.
b : Won't the lid hold? | Want to catch it?
a : I'm happier checking the lid with both eyes open. | Want to hear it retreat before I take another step.

scene exchange9
when topic=memories
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : There's a sum due at the next new moon. | I'm not in the habit of counting another wolf's coin.
b : Did you borrow it for stock? | And your own?
a : The date's quite public in the sky. The reason stays in my pocket. | The less I have the more often it gets counted.

scene exchange10
when topic=home
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A high stair keeps me honest about what I carry. | I put the light things underneath the rest of my bundle.
b : Too much trouble to climb twice? | Won't they get crushed?
a : Too little space in my arms to carry two lies and a parcel. | The heavy thing stays in my paw under my own close inspection.

scene exchange11
when topic=work self.job=laborer self.boss
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I can ask #self.boss# what's to be cried before the stalls open. | I keep my private worries off everybody else's price call.
b : Do you repeat it exactly? | Never a slip?
a : Depends how many breaths the description takes. | If I hesitate I go back to colour and size. Safe ground.

scene exchange12
when topic=gossip here.gossip=yes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I heard #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. I could cry that quite handsomely. | A rumour runs up a crowded flight without taking a breath.
b : Are you going to? | Do you let the rumour past?
a : No. I cry cloth. Cloth doesn't suffer from a wrong description the way a living wolf can. | I let it pass and see if any witness comes along behind.

scene exchange13
when topic=times world.times=hard|lean
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Hard times change what my big voice sells. | When the market's lean I can hear an empty purse opening.
b : Do prices go down? | What sound gives it away?
a : More bargains cut from the ends and fewer full lengths. | A little rustle followed by a very long pause.

scene exchange14
when topic=dreams
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd like a week's calls that start and finish with paid-up coin. | I dream a stair has a flat bit where an awkward question ought to be.
b : How would you spend the quieter hours? | Do you stop on it?
a : Eat one whole oatcake without figuring the next one first. | I've never quite decided till I wake.

scene exchange15
when topic=land here.region=ridgemere
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : My map of the city would show stairs in pairs. | I could point out the long stair by the voices below it.
b : And the very steep ones? | How?
a : I'd put a small drawing of a closed mouth halfway up. | The first shout carries up clean. The answer coming down gets chopped by the turns.

scene exchange16
when topic=health
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I stop a long cry just before my throat feels dry. | Two steps give my knees a comfortable swing.
b : How do you learn when? | Even on the way down?
a : By going past it once and having an unwanted day of whispering. | Coming down I give the stones a chance to prove themselves singly.

scene exchange17
when topic=day
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : My best breath sits ready just behind the ribs. | I close the day by saying a whole sentence softly.
b : Does that make a long call? | What sentence?
a : It makes a calm one. Long needn't mean anything but tired. | Usually something ordinary like 'the snap on my bag has held.'

scene exchange18
when topic=faith
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I don't make stretching a coin the Bright One's business. | A chapel and a market both have places where a voice carries.
b : What do you ask? | Do you speak loud there too?
a : Sense to know which wolf needs the next one most. | No. The market's paying for it. The chapel isn't.

story tale1 [topic=work self.job=laborer]
  : I cried up a bolt of cloth with such a carrying voice that a customer took the colour for a direction and turned down a side lane.
  : I tried giving the right call again, which naturally sent the poor soul farther off.
  b : How did you bring the customer back?
  : Held the patterned end over my head and kept my bright ideas behind my teeth.

story tale2 [topic=travel]
  : One stair I used for practice had a missing tread. I learned the entire ascent as a pleasing little sequence of pairs, skipping the gap clean.
  : The missing tread got mended. I went up by memory and stumbled on solid wood.
  b : Did the repaired stair hurt you?
  : Mostly it hurt my pride. I give a good repair a nod now when I pass.

story tale3 [topic=pastimes self.likes=riddles]
  : I once set a question in two halves at two far corners of one street. Reaching the second corner I realised I'd changed the answer in my head.
  : Both versions quite neatly fitted the first half.
  b : Which one did you give?
  : I walked back, collected the original question and sat down with my oatcake. An unsupervised riddle can get expensive in shoe leather.

rule @call1
when concept=bark working=yes self.job=laborer
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Clear pattern up high for the far row! | Bright strip at an honestly marked length!

rule @call2
when concept=bark here.time=dawn
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Bells can wait. My voice is still putting its coat on. | First step wants testing before the pair.

rule @call3
when concept=bark self.likes=oatcakes
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Crisp edge, sound middle. There's a bite worth keeping. | Crumbs stay in the wrapper till the climb's done.

rule @call4
when concept=bark here.weather=rain
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Keep the lower end of the sample clear of the drip. | Dry cloth gets seen from farther off.

dlg @1 resident.hub : My lower voice costs nothing. You've got that one.
dlg @2 resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : #topic.player#, our voices don't need their public pitch here.
dlg @3 resident.hub [here.time=night] : My voice works more quietly up here after dark.
dlg @4 resident.hub [pair.disposition=wary|hostile] : I can hear your question with the purse strings shut.
dlg @1 resident.job [self.job=laborer] : I cry wares where the market's at its loudest. Pattern, colour, length and price, in one lungful if possible.
dlg @2 resident.job : I give my paid hours the voice they bought and keep a private one for later.
dlg @1 resident.news [world.news] : From somewhere beyond my last call comes #world.news#.
dlg @1 resident.gossip [here.gossip=yes] : The claim came to my ear as #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. That isn't a sworn account.
dlg @1 resident.bye : Keep one good breath for the last rise.
graft resident.hub
choice Can you fit a riddle in a market cry? -> price_riddle
node price_riddle
say Easy. One bolt cast two shadows, one red and one blue. That's the question I sing. The price gets said in an ordinary voice.
free
choice What's the answer to the riddle? -> price_riddle_again
choice Goodbye. -> bye
node price_riddle_again
say Cloth woven different on each face. It draws the eye twice, which is all I can fairly promise a seller.
choice I'll look at both faces. -> hub
choice Goodbye. -> bye
